<title>USA: US Sept leading indicators +0.1 pct - Conference Bd.</title>
<headline>US Sept leading indicators +0.1 pct - Conference Bd.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Conference Board index of leading, coincident and lagging indicators (1987=100) and percent changes from previous months, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>    -			Index---Sept  Aug-Rev from  July</p>
<p> Leading Indicators    103.5   0.1    0.2   0.2     0.2</p>
<p> Coincident Indicators 121.9   0.2    0.2   0.4     0.2</p>
<p> Lagging Indicators    102.8   0.3   -0.1   0.1     0.4</p>
<p>Following are components of the index of leading</p>
<p>indicators with net contributions to monthly changes.</p>
<p>    -			   Sept   Aug--Rev from   July</p>
<p> Average Workweek	   0.04   0.04   0.04    -0.09</p>
<p> Initial Jobless Claims  -0.10   0.07   0.07     0.13</p>
<p> Consumer Goods Orders    0.05  -0.05  -0.03     0.09</p>
<p> Slower Deliveries	 -0.10   0.05   0.05    -0.08</p>
<p> Plant, Equipment Orders  0.11  -0.08  -0.08     0.06</p>
<p>    -			   Sept   Aug--Rev from   July</p>
<p> Building Permits	  -0.02  -0.03  -0.03     0.04</p>
<p> Unfilled Orders	   -0.06  -0.14  -0.10    -0.02</p>
<p> Materials Prices	   0.11   0.16   0.18     0.11</p>
<p> Stock Prices		 0.05   0.08   0.08    -0.10</p>
<p> Money Supply		-0.01   0.04   0.02    -0.02</p>
<p> Consumer Expectations    0.05   0.01   0.01     0.04</p>
<p>The September advance marks the eighth straight monthly rise.</p>
<p>The board changed the release date for the October report on leading indicators to December 3 at 0830 EST/1330 GMT from December 2.</p>
</text>
